parents of the 30 year old man killed in  a motorcycle crash flew into town to  bring their son's remains back home this  crash happened just after midnight  yesterday on southbound 95 right by ann  road shutting down the freeway for  several hours victoria saha spoke with  the family and has more tonight  mom kimberly davis holds on to the lost  belongings touched by her sons  30-year-old aaron barris too emotional  to show her face he rode every chance he  got he loved to ride nevada state police  say barris was riding on the on ramp of  u.s 95 at a high rate of speed when his  2020 suzuki motorcycle wheel locked  causing it to skid and hit the median  barrier wall  barris was thrown off and hit a light  pole  he looked for that bike for a long time  and he just got it  about six or eight months ago this is  video bearers posted on his facebook  page a few months ago his mom said he  had just finished his shift working  security at the wind just after midnight  tuesday when the crash happened barris  was an army veteran and worked at his  local sheriff's department in florida  recently moving to vegas to be closer to  his son colt he loved his son more than  anything  he loved his family  he would do anything for anybody dave is  recalling her last conversation with her  son monday afternoon he saw something at  the store that made me laugh and he  facetimed me and showed me and  just like love you mom talk to you  tomorrow victoria saha live local now  the family has set up a gofundme to help  with building a trust fund for bruce's  son you can find that link over on our  website at 8newsnow.com
 

